From: ae-automation-bot <ae-automation-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 11:16:11 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 047/202] [ae-patch] Drop Claude Code's own subagents and
 technical strings from the usage popover

Reid sent a screenshot of the usage popover's detailed breakdown on
2026-10-15. Its collaborators were Claude Code's own subagents
("general-purpose:a45b4b1759d6fb802"), each "Unavailable" with a sentence
and a repeated "Claude Code" line, since they run inside Claude Code's
process and report no context of their own.

- Child sessions labelled omnigent.wrapper=claude-code-native-ui-subagent
  leave the collaborators list, before the six-row cap.
- A collaborator is named by its task summary or title, never a bare
  "type:hexid"; "Collaborator" otherwise.
- A collaborator without a reading is one line, "No reading yet", with the
  reason in its tooltip. This session's row keeps one short line.
- Model ids read as names: "claude-opus-5-5[1m]" is "Opus 5.5".
- A Claude Code session on a 1M window shows "About 524k until
  auto-compact" under the context bar: Claude Code compacts a native 1M
  window at about 967k tokens by default.
- A plan with no reading says "No reading yet"; what to do about it (the
  relay timer, codex login) moved to the tooltip.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
